  "final_text": "## Summary\n\nI ran EXCLURAD for the \u03b7 channel at W = 1.54 GeV, Q\u00b2 = 1.3207 GeV\u00b2, cos \u03b8* = 0.341379, \u03c6* = 36\u00b0 using the standard CLAS12 settings (model=3 EtaMAID, full O(\u03b1) RC, bmom=6.53 GeV, ivec=1 recoil proton, vcut=0.166 GeV\u00b2).\n\n**Note on setup:** the executable hardcodes `open(unit=5, file='input.dat')`, so it ignores stdin redirection \u2014 I had to write the kinematics directly into `eta/input.dat` to run the job (restored the original template afterward).\n\n**Results:**\n- **\u03c3_Born = 0.0008651649** (EXCLURAD's internal units, from `radtot.dat`)\n- **\u03b4 = NaN** \u2014 the full radiative-tail integral (`qqt`/`d01fce`) fails to converge in the narrow collinear-peak sub-region at this specific point. This is fully deterministic and reproducible across repeated runs, so it's a genuine numerical breakdown of the integrator for this kinematic point, not a setup issue.\n\nI reported `delta: null` in `outcome.json` (written to the working directory) with an explanation, and included \u03c3_Born exactly as EXCLURAD wrote it, unrounded.",
